WEBVTT

00:03.485 --> 00:07.021
Hey Lyndsey,
just calling to say good night.

00:07.023 --> 00:09.356
Oh, oh,
you're in bed already?

00:09.358 --> 00:13.778
So, uh,
what are you wearing?

00:13.780 --> 00:14.962
Really?

00:14.964 --> 00:16.497
What kind of sweat pants?

00:17.666 --> 00:21.636
Ooh,
big, old gray ones.

00:21.638 --> 00:25.256
Is it just me or are you
getting turned on, too?

00:25.258 --> 00:28.342
It's...j-j-just me?

00:28.344 --> 00:29.310
Well, that's fine.

00:29.312 --> 00:31.896
I do some of my best work alone.

00:31.898 --> 00:34.215
All right, all right,
go to sleep.

00:34.217 --> 00:35.266
I love you.

00:35.268 --> 00:36.517
Do you love...?

00:38.103 --> 00:39.770
I know she does.

00:43.609 --> 00:44.942
Oh, great.

00:44.944 --> 00:45.943
(sighs)

00:48.614 --> 00:50.481
(screams)

00:53.001 --> 00:54.452
Uh-oh, uh...

00:54.454 --> 00:56.671
(sighs)

00:58.790 --> 00:59.840
Oh!

00:59.842 --> 01:01.959
Oh, no, no, no.

01:01.961 --> 01:04.212
No, I can't burn down
another house.

01:08.350 --> 01:11.936
(shrieking)

01:21.063 --> 01:22.980
WALDEN:
Alan?

01:24.700 --> 01:26.784
Oh, hi.

01:26.786 --> 01:28.819
Um, just making some toast.

01:33.909 --> 01:35.459
Huh.

01:35.461 --> 01:37.411
Wonder what happened.

01:40.966 --> 01:43.834
♪ Men, men, men, men, manly men,
men, men ♪

01:43.836 --> 01:47.054
♪ Men, men, men, manly men, men, men ♪
♪ Ooh

01:47.056 --> 01:50.224
♪ Men, men, men, men, manly men ♪
♪ Ooh

01:50.226 --> 01:52.343
♪ Ooh-ooh-ooh,
ooh-ohh, ooh-ooh... ♪

01:52.345 --> 01:54.845
♪ Men, men, men, men, manly men,
men, men ♪

01:54.847 --> 01:57.848
♪ Ooh
♪ Men, men, men, manly men, men, men ♪

01:57.850 --> 02:01.969
♪ Ah.
♪ Men.

02:01.994 --> 02:05.994
&lt;font color="#00FF00">♪ Two and a Half Men 10x18 ♪&lt;/font>
&lt;font color="#00FFFF">The 9:04 From Pemberton&lt;/font>
Original Air Date on March 7, 2013

02:06.019 --> 02:11.019
== sync, corrected by &lt;font color="#00FF00">elderman&lt;/font> ==

02:17.686 --> 02:18.753
Morning.

02:18.755 --> 02:19.921
Hey.

02:19.923 --> 02:22.056
Sorry again about last night.
(awkward laugh)

02:22.058 --> 02:23.341
Sorry about what?

02:23.343 --> 02:25.409
The fact that
my date and I came home

02:25.411 --> 02:27.245
last night to find
a middle-aged man

02:27.247 --> 02:29.681
spraying water
all over my kitchen

02:29.683 --> 02:32.583
in his tighty
not-so-whities?

02:32.585 --> 02:35.303
I was putting out a fire.

02:35.305 --> 02:37.422
I'm a hero.

02:37.424 --> 02:38.589
Really?

02:38.591 --> 02:40.308
'Cause it looked like you were
posing for

02:40.310 --> 02:42.477
the World's Most Disturbing
Firemen calendar.

02:44.647 --> 02:45.446
Okay, okay, I get it.

02:45.448 --> 02:46.931
You're a little upset.

02:46.933 --> 02:50.034
But I have something that will
make you feel better.

02:50.036 --> 02:51.819
♪ Ta-da.

02:51.821 --> 02:53.788
I went out to the drugstore

02:53.790 --> 02:56.207
and bought you a new toaster
to replace the old one.

02:58.878 --> 03:00.778
The other one was better.

03:01.247 --> 03:02.964
Better?!

03:02.966 --> 03:05.166
This is the Toastblaster Deluxe.

03:05.168 --> 03:08.219
This is the best thing to happen
to sliced bread since...

03:08.221 --> 03:09.954
sliced bread.

03:09.956 --> 03:12.423
But mine had glass walls,

03:12.425 --> 03:14.676
so you could watch the
toast turn tropical brown.

03:14.678 --> 03:17.145
It was like a... little...

03:17.147 --> 03:19.731
bread tanning booth.

03:21.767 --> 03:23.017
Well, check this out, you know.

03:23.019 --> 03:24.802
Light, dark.

03:24.804 --> 03:26.404
Dark...

03:26.406 --> 03:28.639
light.

03:28.641 --> 03:32.076
Okay, that's, uh...

03:32.078 --> 03:33.328
that-that's supposed to happen.

03:33.330 --> 03:35.196
That's ac-- that's actually
a safety feature.

03:35.198 --> 03:37.115
You know,
common courtesy dictates

03:37.117 --> 03:39.150
that if you're
gonna use my stuff

03:39.152 --> 03:40.484
and break my stuff,

03:40.486 --> 03:41.669
that you replace my stuff

03:41.671 --> 03:43.922
with equally awesome stuff.

03:43.924 --> 03:46.457
This-this-this
is what would happen

03:46.459 --> 03:49.093
if my toaster took a crap.

03:50.796 --> 03:52.213
What are you talking about?

03:52.215 --> 03:53.932
This is a
perfectly good toaster.

03:53.934 --> 03:56.467
Look, okay, you know what?
I'll prove it to you.

04:00.005 --> 04:01.639
Hope you're hungry.

04:01.641 --> 04:04.692
(loud buzzing)

04:05.728 --> 04:10.114
(loudly):
Listen to that baby purr!

04:10.116 --> 04:13.184
(loudly):
I hate you.

04:17.740 --> 04:19.824
BERTA:
By the way,

04:19.826 --> 04:20.792
in case I forget.

04:20.794 --> 04:22.794
I might be a little
late on Monday.

04:22.796 --> 04:23.694
Oh, no problem.

04:23.696 --> 04:25.079
When should
I expect you?

04:25.081 --> 04:27.882
Wednesday.

04:27.884 --> 04:30.568
Should I dock you
for the time you miss?

04:30.570 --> 04:32.503
I wouldn't.

04:34.690 --> 04:36.758
(sighs)

04:43.899 --> 04:44.899
Here you go.

04:44.901 --> 04:46.401
What's this?

04:46.403 --> 04:48.319
I went to the store
and I asked them,

04:48.321 --> 04:50.154
"What is the
stupidest thing I can buy?"

04:50.156 --> 04:51.439
and they
gave me this toaster.

04:51.441 --> 04:52.556
Enjoy.

04:52.558 --> 04:54.659
You know,
you didn't have to do that.

04:54.661 --> 04:56.560
Ah, you made it pretty clear
that I did.

04:56.562 --> 04:59.897
In fact, I forwent replacing
my cell phone to buy this.

04:59.899 --> 05:02.000
"Forwent"?

05:02.002 --> 05:04.619
It's a word.

05:04.621 --> 05:05.753
Well, I appreciate it.

05:05.755 --> 05:07.171
Thank you.

05:07.173 --> 05:09.740
Uh, and you don't have to worry
about me ruining that one,

05:09.742 --> 05:11.175
because
I will never use it.

05:11.177 --> 05:12.743
Okay, stop being ridiculous.

05:12.745 --> 05:13.761
(scoffing)

05:13.763 --> 05:15.296
You want to know what's
ridiculous?

05:15.298 --> 05:16.764
A glass toaster.

05:16.766 --> 05:17.598
What's next?

05:17.600 --> 05:18.599
A glass toilet,

05:18.601 --> 05:21.219
so you can wave good-bye
to the toast?

05:25.074 --> 05:27.275
How about a glass front door

05:27.277 --> 05:29.027
so I can wave good-bye to you?

05:29.029 --> 05:31.946
Oh, please!
You would be lost without me.

05:31.948 --> 05:35.316
I would be lost without &lt;i>you?&lt;/i>
Yeah.

05:35.318 --> 05:39.603
Okay, the only thing that you've
brought into my life

05:39.605 --> 05:41.706
is an oil-leaking Volvo,

05:41.708 --> 05:44.208
a musty smell in
my guest room

05:44.210 --> 05:46.044
and the word "forwent."

05:46.046 --> 05:48.329
It is the past tense
of "forgo."

05:48.331 --> 05:49.831
Edify yourself, sir.

05:50.949 --> 05:52.967
And have you noticed

05:52.969 --> 05:55.136
that all the people in your life
come and go,

05:55.138 --> 05:56.471
but I am the one constant?

05:56.473 --> 05:57.505
I am always here.

05:57.507 --> 05:59.173
Maybe the reason
they come and go

05:59.175 --> 06:01.625
is because you are always here.

06:01.627 --> 06:03.511
When a woman dumps you,
who picks up the pieces?

06:03.513 --> 06:04.512
Alan Harper.

06:04.514 --> 06:06.130
And who picks up the check?

06:06.132 --> 06:07.148
Walden Schmidt.

06:07.150 --> 06:08.632
(scoffs)
Of course, of course.

06:08.634 --> 06:09.800
Pull out the money card.

06:09.802 --> 06:11.402
They're called credit cards.

06:11.404 --> 06:13.154
Edify yourself, sir.

06:13.156 --> 06:14.655
Okay, if-if-if
this is how you think,

06:14.657 --> 06:16.524
then I don't even know why
I'm living here.

06:16.526 --> 06:19.077
Oh, I do: because it's free!

06:19.079 --> 06:20.528
Okay, okay, maybe I should go.

06:20.530 --> 06:21.479
Maybe you should.

06:21.481 --> 06:22.296
Fine.
Fine.

06:22.298 --> 06:24.465
Okay.
Okay.

06:24.467 --> 06:25.566
I am not bluffing.

06:25.568 --> 06:26.701
Me neither.

06:26.703 --> 06:28.920
This is me
opening the door.

06:28.922 --> 06:30.788
This is me watching.

06:30.790 --> 06:32.073
This is me leaving forever.

06:32.075 --> 06:34.959
This is me waving good-bye.

06:37.880 --> 06:40.531
And this is me homeless.

06:40.533 --> 06:42.550
♪ &lt;i>Men...&lt;/i> ♪

06:42.552 --> 06:43.935
You know what the problem is?

06:43.937 --> 06:46.020
Walden doesn't appreciate what
I bring to the party.

06:46.022 --> 06:48.672
I've never seen you bring
anything to a party.

06:48.674 --> 06:51.392
Except a ziplock bag
to steal the shrimp.

06:51.394 --> 06:52.727
Whose side are you on?

06:52.729 --> 06:54.278
Yours, of course.

06:54.280 --> 06:56.013
Listen, I know you're upset,

06:56.015 --> 06:58.316
but I'm sure you two
lovebirds will kiss and make up.

06:58.318 --> 06:59.567
No, not happening.

06:59.569 --> 07:01.569
He does not want me back,
and I'm not going back.

07:01.571 --> 07:02.453
You're not?
No.

07:02.455 --> 07:04.288
I have my self-respect.

07:05.124 --> 07:06.791
I do.

07:06.793 --> 07:08.526
So where are you gonna live?

07:08.528 --> 07:10.578
(chuckling): Where am I
going to live? You're cute.

07:10.580 --> 07:11.996
(chuckling):
Thanks.

07:11.998 --> 07:13.080
So where are
you gonna live?

07:13.082 --> 07:14.582
Seriously?

07:14.584 --> 07:16.700
Alan, I want
to live with you.

07:16.702 --> 07:17.835
But when you move in,

07:17.837 --> 07:19.253
I want it to be
because I'm your first choice,

07:19.255 --> 07:20.538
not your last resort.

07:20.540 --> 07:23.040
You are my first choice.
I'm your only choice.

07:23.042 --> 07:25.676
My one and only choice.

07:25.678 --> 07:27.645
Until Walden asks
you to move back.

07:27.647 --> 07:28.980
Oh, please!

07:28.982 --> 07:31.315
I-I am offended that you could
even suggest such a thing.

07:31.317 --> 07:32.567
You are the woman I love;

07:32.569 --> 07:35.153
the woman I want to spend
the rest of my life with.

07:35.155 --> 07:37.388
Aw... you're right, sweetie.

07:37.390 --> 07:40.408
I'm sorry. You can move in.
Oh, thank you.

07:40.410 --> 07:41.946
It'll be nice to
share the place with you.

07:41.947 --> 07:42.908
Yeah, it's gonna be great.

07:42.912 --> 07:44.862
And we can split all the bills
right down the middle.

07:44.864 --> 07:46.063
Ah...

07:47.032 --> 07:50.168
Oh, come on,
you don't want my money.

07:50.170 --> 07:52.036
You're an
independent woman.

07:52.038 --> 07:53.704
Walk proud.

07:53.706 --> 07:57.875
Walk over
to this door and let me back in.

07:57.877 --> 07:59.510
HERB:
Hey, Alan.

07:59.512 --> 08:03.381
Oh, God! Herb!

08:03.383 --> 08:04.382
What-what are you doing?

08:04.384 --> 08:05.550
Neighborhood watch.

08:05.552 --> 08:06.584
Oh, that's nice.

08:06.586 --> 08:07.718
I-I didn't even know
there was one.

08:07.720 --> 08:09.053
There isn't.

08:09.055 --> 08:11.138
So, uh, you and
Lyndsey have a little tiff?

08:11.140 --> 08:15.476
Oh, uh, not really a tiff,
as much as, uh...

08:15.478 --> 08:17.445
Hey, are you
still rattling around

08:17.447 --> 08:19.113
in that big old
house all by yourself?

08:19.115 --> 08:21.432
Yeah, I don't think Judith's
ever coming back.

08:21.434 --> 08:23.234
That's terrific...

08:23.236 --> 08:25.620
...ly sad.

08:25.622 --> 08:26.954
You know what?

08:26.956 --> 08:29.156
At a time like this, you-you
should not be alone.

08:29.158 --> 08:31.492
Let's go over to your place
and have a few beers.

08:31.494 --> 08:33.277
You're a good friend, Alan.

08:33.279 --> 08:34.945
What can I say?
I'm a giver.

08:34.947 --> 08:38.049
Say, do you still have
the hide-a-bed in the den?

08:38.051 --> 08:40.167
♪ &lt;i>Men...&lt;/i> ♪

08:40.169 --> 08:44.922
All right, I packed up
all Zippy's stuff.

08:44.924 --> 08:46.674
It's sad.

08:46.676 --> 08:50.961
His entire life
fits into one duffel bag.

08:50.963 --> 08:54.315
What's even sadder
is it's my duffel bag.

08:54.317 --> 08:56.800
He's coming back;
you know that, right?

08:56.802 --> 08:57.985
No, he's not.

08:57.987 --> 08:59.970
He is a human boomerang.

08:59.972 --> 09:02.806
He's going to circle around,
break a window,

09:02.808 --> 09:05.476
and land right on your couch.

09:05.478 --> 09:08.112
(doorbell rings)

09:14.836 --> 09:16.287
Open a window
in the kitchen,

09:16.289 --> 09:18.122
maybe he'll just
go straight through.

09:21.710 --> 09:22.760
Alan.

09:22.762 --> 09:24.095
Walden.

09:24.097 --> 09:26.514
Don't worry, I'm just here
to pick up my things

09:26.516 --> 09:27.682
and then I'll be on my way.

09:27.684 --> 09:29.684
Where you heading,
Zippy, back to Mommy's?

09:29.686 --> 09:31.385
Living with my mother--

09:31.387 --> 09:33.187
that's pretty pathetic,
isn't it?

09:33.189 --> 09:34.972
No, for your information,

09:34.974 --> 09:36.641
I am living
with my ex-wife's ex-husband

09:36.643 --> 09:40.261
at my ex-house.

09:40.263 --> 09:42.380
Yeah, that's not pathetic.

09:42.382 --> 09:44.832
I packed your things for you.
(clears throat)

09:44.834 --> 09:46.284
Oh.

09:46.286 --> 09:48.235
I presume this is everything?

09:48.237 --> 09:49.820
You presume correct.
Hmm.

09:49.822 --> 09:51.489
Your clothes,
your toaster

09:51.491 --> 09:53.958
and your expired
Mexican boner pills.

09:58.997 --> 10:01.532
Is it lonely up there, Walden?

10:02.718 --> 10:06.554
Is it lonely
on your cloud of judgment?

10:06.556 --> 10:09.473
I don't know, maybe you could
leave, so I could find out.

10:09.475 --> 10:12.176
All right,
then, good-bye.

10:13.812 --> 10:15.730
Berta, are you crying?

10:15.732 --> 10:18.099
(crying):
I can't help it.

10:18.101 --> 10:20.384
I'm just so damn happy.

10:21.086 --> 10:23.821
♪ &lt;i>Men...&lt;/i> ♪

10:30.557 --> 10:32.124
♪ &lt;i>Men...&lt;/i> ♪

10:32.126 --> 10:34.043
Here you go.

10:34.045 --> 10:37.179
Two eggs over easy,
silver dollar pancakes,

10:37.181 --> 10:41.450
apple wood smoked bacon
and whole grain toast.

10:41.452 --> 10:43.886
(chuckling):
This is delightful, Alan.

10:43.888 --> 10:46.204
You really know
how to spoil your man.

10:47.474 --> 10:49.258
And you know
how to flatter yours.

10:50.209 --> 10:52.228
Wow, it seems
like just yesterday

10:52.230 --> 10:53.896
I was living
here with Judith.

10:53.898 --> 10:55.014
Only difference now is,

10:55.016 --> 10:57.233
I actually have a
chance at getting laid.

10:57.235 --> 10:59.935
Well, if dinner's
as good as breakfast,

10:59.937 --> 11:01.270
you've got
more than a chance.

11:01.272 --> 11:02.905
(laughing)

11:02.907 --> 11:03.906
Seriously,
I-I really appreciate

11:03.908 --> 11:05.241
you letting
me stay here.

11:05.243 --> 11:07.109
Ah, well, it's nice to
have someone around again.

11:07.111 --> 11:09.194
It's been a little
lonely since Judith left.

11:09.196 --> 11:11.247
I found it lonely
even when Judith was here.

11:11.249 --> 11:13.899
Mm... Yeah, I've
been watching TV alone

11:13.901 --> 11:15.868
and drinking alone.

11:15.870 --> 11:17.653
I even painted a
moustache on the bathroom mirror

11:17.655 --> 11:19.004
so I'd have
someone to talk to.

11:19.006 --> 11:21.907
R... Really?

11:21.909 --> 11:24.426
Yeah. I call him Javier.

11:24.428 --> 11:26.845
(Latin accent): Don't worry, Herb,
you're better off.

11:26.847 --> 11:30.182
"Yudith," she's a "beetch."

11:30.184 --> 11:32.601
Can't argue with Javier.

11:32.603 --> 11:35.721
No, no, I wouldn't--
he's got a fiery Latin temper.

11:35.723 --> 11:38.090
And a machete.

11:42.428 --> 11:44.780
Um, l-let me ask you something.

11:45.598 --> 11:47.432
Does Herb have a machete?

11:52.489 --> 11:54.523
(footsteps approaching)

11:54.525 --> 11:55.724
Morning.

11:55.726 --> 11:57.209
Morning.

11:57.211 --> 11:59.912
Hey, Berta, knock, knock.

11:59.914 --> 12:00.863
Who's there?

12:00.865 --> 12:01.947
Not Alan.

12:01.949 --> 12:03.615
(laughing)

12:03.617 --> 12:05.584
Free at last, Walden.

12:05.586 --> 12:07.753
Thank God Almighty,
we're free at last.

12:07.755 --> 12:11.223
Yeah. Although it is
a little quieter around here.

12:11.225 --> 12:13.175
Get a dog-- then it
won't seem so weird

12:13.177 --> 12:15.144
when you catch him
trying to lick himself.

12:16.179 --> 12:17.646
Hey, Berta?
Yeah?

12:17.648 --> 12:19.815
What do you think about
turning Alan's room

12:19.817 --> 12:21.133
into a home gym?

12:21.135 --> 12:23.652
Well, I was thinking about
trying to grow pot in there,

12:23.654 --> 12:25.020
but okay.

12:25.022 --> 12:26.689
Hey, Berta?

12:26.691 --> 12:27.589
Yeah?

12:27.591 --> 12:29.575
What's going on with you?

12:29.577 --> 12:30.976
What do you mean?

12:30.978 --> 12:32.778
I don't know. Like...

12:32.780 --> 12:34.496
how's your family?

12:34.498 --> 12:36.532
Incarcerated.
(laughs)

12:36.534 --> 12:38.784
That's funny.

12:38.786 --> 12:40.452
Okay. Good talk.

12:40.454 --> 12:42.454
Hey... Berta?

12:42.456 --> 12:43.706
Yeah?

12:43.708 --> 12:44.707
Knock, knock.

12:44.709 --> 12:46.175
Who's there?

12:46.177 --> 12:47.926
It's Walden. Let me in.

12:50.547 --> 12:52.765
What are your hopes?
What are your dreams?

12:52.767 --> 12:55.267
I'm just hoping to get
out of this conversation.

12:55.269 --> 12:56.552
(chuckles)

12:56.554 --> 12:58.270
You're... you're
on fire today.

12:58.272 --> 12:59.555
Yeah.

12:59.557 --> 13:00.839
Hey, Berta?

13:00.841 --> 13:04.059
Oh, for the love of God, what?

13:04.061 --> 13:05.310
I like your vest.

13:06.679 --> 13:08.197
Thanks.

13:08.199 --> 13:11.116
Where'd you get it, like,
the vest store or something?

13:12.402 --> 13:15.170
Thank God I'm high.

13:23.997 --> 13:25.464
Easy, easy.

13:25.466 --> 13:28.366
Sound the horn, let
the townfolk know you're coming.

13:28.368 --> 13:30.469
(train whistle blows)

13:30.471 --> 13:34.423
The 9:04 from Pemberton,
now arriving on track one.

13:34.425 --> 13:36.141
Right on time.

13:36.143 --> 13:38.560
I-I had no idea
this was so much fun.

13:38.562 --> 13:39.511
I know.

13:39.513 --> 13:41.213
(gasps)
Look, Alan...

13:41.215 --> 13:43.899
the McDougal boy's
coming home from college.

13:45.018 --> 13:47.019
What a reunion this will be.

13:47.021 --> 13:49.054
Welcome home, Jimmy!

13:49.056 --> 13:51.723
Wow, you've, uh, created
your own little world here.

13:51.725 --> 13:53.692
Oh, yeah,
and this world's perfect.

13:53.694 --> 13:55.861
Well... almost perfect.

13:56.613 --> 13:57.830
Jimmy's brother Bobby

13:57.832 --> 14:00.282
got a little too close
to the tracks one night.

14:00.284 --> 14:03.235
Him and his friends were playing
chicken with a freight train.

14:04.671 --> 14:07.923
They found his letterman jacket
three towns away.

14:07.925 --> 14:09.875
Oh, no.
Yeah.

14:09.877 --> 14:11.677
Engineer Stan never got over it.

14:11.679 --> 14:13.462
He stopped talking to Helen.

14:13.464 --> 14:16.014
He just sits in his room
and paints.

14:18.768 --> 14:21.720
Huh. That's, uh...
that's disturbing.

14:21.722 --> 14:24.356
On a couple of levels.

14:24.358 --> 14:26.258
You know it's
so nice having you.

14:26.260 --> 14:29.728
I don't know why, but train
enthusiasts tend to be loners.

14:29.730 --> 14:32.314
Yeah. It's a mystery.

14:32.316 --> 14:34.199
(phone rings)

14:34.201 --> 14:35.534
Hello?

14:35.536 --> 14:38.070
Hey, Herb. It's Walden.

14:38.072 --> 14:39.705
Oh. Hey, hold on a sec.

14:39.707 --> 14:41.439
Uh, I got to take this;
it's the office.

14:41.441 --> 14:43.459
No problem. I was thinking
of heading over to the bar car

14:43.461 --> 14:45.610
to pick us up a couple
of frosty brews. You want one?

14:45.612 --> 14:47.129
Oh, make mine a root beer.

14:47.131 --> 14:48.881
This town's seen enough tragedy.

14:52.218 --> 14:53.252
(door closes)

14:53.254 --> 14:54.269
Hey, what's up?

14:54.271 --> 14:55.504
Is Alan there?

14:55.506 --> 14:57.806
Uh, actually, no,
I haven't seen him all day.

14:57.808 --> 14:59.358
I was really hoping
to talk to him.

14:59.360 --> 15:01.977
You can't talk
to a person that's not here.

15:01.979 --> 15:04.429
Unless you draw a mustache
on the mirror.

15:04.431 --> 15:05.931
What?

15:05.933 --> 15:07.399
Is there a message
I can give him?

15:07.401 --> 15:09.351
Yeah, just tell him
I think I overreacted,

15:09.353 --> 15:11.153
and have him give me a call.

15:11.688 --> 15:13.405
Done and done. Bye-bye.

15:13.407 --> 15:15.357
Everything okay at the office?

15:15.359 --> 15:17.743
Uh, actually, it,
uh, it wasn't work.

15:17.745 --> 15:18.744
No?

15:18.746 --> 15:19.811
It was the, uh,

15:19.813 --> 15:20.996
president of the railroad.

15:20.998 --> 15:22.981
He asked me to give you this.

15:24.483 --> 15:26.084
Congratulations, Conductor Alan!

15:26.086 --> 15:27.419
Oh, my God! Thank you!

15:27.421 --> 15:28.754
Now, let's get
that coal car unloaded

15:28.756 --> 15:30.672
and head over to the diner.

15:30.674 --> 15:32.741
Take a look at the new waitress.
Ooh!

15:32.743 --> 15:33.709
Word around town is,

15:33.711 --> 15:35.711
(whispers):
she goes all the way.

15:43.937 --> 15:45.888
(computer beeping)

15:45.890 --> 15:47.306
Hey, Jake!

15:47.308 --> 15:48.307
Walden.

15:48.309 --> 15:50.809
How are you?
What's going on, buddy?

15:50.811 --> 15:53.612
Not much.
Is my dad there?

15:53.614 --> 15:56.231
No. He actually moved out.

15:56.233 --> 15:58.951
(laughing):
Good one!

15:58.953 --> 16:00.052
No, I'm-I'm serious.

16:00.054 --> 16:02.454
We got in a fight,
and he left.

16:02.456 --> 16:05.290
My dad left that house?

16:05.292 --> 16:08.693
Yeah. We got in a fight, 'cause
he bought a cheap toaster.

16:08.695 --> 16:10.028
W-Wait, wait.

16:10.030 --> 16:13.415
&lt;i>And&lt;/i> he bought something?

16:13.417 --> 16:17.135
Yeah. And I didn't show
any appreciation for it.

16:17.137 --> 16:19.972
He bought something
with his own money?

16:19.974 --> 16:22.641
I know. I shouldn't
have screamed at him.

16:22.643 --> 16:25.644
I-I should have
thrown him a parade.

16:25.646 --> 16:29.314
Wait a second,
am I being punk'd?

16:30.433 --> 16:32.351
Hey, you know, I got an idea.

16:32.353 --> 16:34.987
Um, you know, just 'cause your
dad doesn't live here anymore

16:34.989 --> 16:37.856
doesn't mean that you couldn't
come stay for a couple of days.

16:37.858 --> 16:39.157
And do what?

16:39.159 --> 16:41.827
I don't know,
like hang out, do guy stuff.

16:41.829 --> 16:44.496
We could go to a bar
and get drunk.

16:44.498 --> 16:46.915
Mm, I'm only 19; I can't drink.

16:46.917 --> 16:49.251
Well, fine,
we could just get high.

16:49.253 --> 16:53.038
Dude, just call my dad and tell
him you want him to come back.

16:53.040 --> 16:55.040
What if he says no?

16:55.042 --> 16:56.959
(snickers, laughs)

16:57.977 --> 17:00.045
Oh, you're serious.

17:00.047 --> 17:02.047
He's not gonna say no.

17:02.049 --> 17:04.099
Where has he even been living?

17:04.101 --> 17:06.584
He moved into you guy's
old house with Herb.

17:06.586 --> 17:08.971
Wow. If there was
a Freeloaders Hall of Fame,

17:08.973 --> 17:11.106
my dad would be living in it.

17:12.358 --> 17:15.027
For free.

17:16.729 --> 17:18.880
(doorbell rings)

17:24.654 --> 17:26.655
Hi, Herb.

17:26.657 --> 17:29.041
Walden. What are
you doing here?

17:29.043 --> 17:30.275
I came to talk to Alan.

17:30.277 --> 17:31.710
Oh.
Sorry, he's not home.

17:31.712 --> 17:33.412
I'll tell him you stopped by.
ALAN: Who's at the door?

17:33.414 --> 17:35.247
Nobody! Go back
in the train room!

17:36.382 --> 17:37.299
Alan?

17:37.301 --> 17:39.051
Walden?

17:39.053 --> 17:41.086
What's, uh,
what's going on?

17:41.088 --> 17:42.620
I wanted to say that I'm sorry.

17:42.622 --> 17:44.289
Really?
Yes.

17:44.291 --> 17:45.424
Super. Hatchet buried.

17:45.426 --> 17:46.624
We'll have you over
for Thanksgiving.

17:46.626 --> 17:48.460
Hold on.

17:48.462 --> 17:52.514
I never meant to make you
feel unwelcome in my home.

17:52.516 --> 17:55.317
Well, Alan has
a new place now.

17:55.319 --> 17:57.402
A place where
he's appreciated.

17:57.404 --> 17:59.521
A place where
he feels safe.

18:00.606 --> 18:03.108
A place where he can cry
himself to sleep at night

18:03.110 --> 18:05.944
without the fear
of being mocked.

18:05.946 --> 18:07.729
Y-You heard that?

18:07.731 --> 18:09.614
There's still
a baby monitor in there.

18:09.616 --> 18:12.617
So you also heard...

18:12.619 --> 18:15.020
Let it go, Alan.

18:16.889 --> 18:18.373
I appreciate you, too.

18:18.375 --> 18:20.926
Th-That's why I've been leaving
messages with Herb for days.

18:20.928 --> 18:22.177
What?!

18:22.179 --> 18:23.512
You haven't gotten them?

18:26.215 --> 18:28.300
Herb...
I'm sorry.

18:28.302 --> 18:29.885
I just wanted a friend.

18:29.887 --> 18:32.971
You know, one who
wasn't trapped in a mirror.

18:34.474 --> 18:36.324
Oh, Herb.

18:36.326 --> 18:37.675
I brought you something.

18:37.677 --> 18:39.194
You did?

18:39.196 --> 18:42.314
You don't happen to
have a toaster, do you?

18:42.316 --> 18:43.815
I have a toaster.

18:43.817 --> 18:47.035
I also have a...
a guest room with a king-size bed

18:47.037 --> 18:49.404
and a new 42-inch
flat-screen TV.

18:49.406 --> 18:50.405
There's no TV in there.

18:50.407 --> 18:52.074
There &lt;i>could&lt;/i> be.

18:52.076 --> 18:54.710
Really?

18:54.712 --> 18:56.578
Your turn.

18:56.580 --> 18:58.914
I'm not gonna
try to buy you.

18:58.916 --> 19:01.166
I mean, you're either
my friend or you're not.

19:01.168 --> 19:03.835
I have no such qualms--
I'll throw in a Blu-ray player.

19:03.837 --> 19:06.388
Wow.
Okay, all right, I'm out of here.

19:06.390 --> 19:08.039
No, no, wait, wait, wait.

19:08.041 --> 19:10.708
(sighs)
Herb...

19:10.710 --> 19:14.179
I-I can't thank you enough
for taking me in,

19:14.181 --> 19:15.814
but...

19:15.816 --> 19:17.432
as you can see...

19:17.434 --> 19:19.151
Walden needs me.

19:19.153 --> 19:21.686
I wouldn't go that far.
Shh...

19:22.822 --> 19:25.657
Let me, uh,
let me get my things.

19:28.077 --> 19:29.611
(sighs)

19:29.613 --> 19:32.364
What is it
about that little guy?

19:32.366 --> 19:35.450
What is it about us
that we're fighting over him?

19:45.991 --> 19:48.274
(funky, sultry music
playing on TV)

19:50.110 --> 19:51.327
Ooh.

19:51.329 --> 19:53.029
What do we have here?

19:53.031 --> 19:57.166
Uh-oh, she's being called
into the boss's office.

19:57.168 --> 20:00.820
Looks like somebody blew
the Johnson account.

20:15.335 --> 20:17.336
WALDEN:
Really, Alan?

20:18.606 --> 20:21.691
Oh, hey, hey! I, uh, I thought
you were still sleeping.

20:21.693 --> 20:25.528
It's 8:00 in the morning!

20:26.363 --> 20:28.180
So?

20:38.492 --> 20:40.192
Hey, Herb. It's Walden.

20:40.194 --> 20:43.379
How would you feel
about shared custody?

20:43.381 --> 20:48.381
== sync, corrected by &lt;font color="#00FF00">elderman&lt;/font> ==
